                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6ccf4310-1d46-4d16-8f7f-8106abdeb732",
                        "entry_id": "cdc9f64b-a5b8-3aaf-819b-4249388c7a5f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "dénotations"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "934ada64-79ce-372d-8bc5-87f421fd39e9",
                        "entry_id": "cdc9f64b-a5b8-3aaf-819b-4249388c7a5f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Action de dénoter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9a00c8f3-e1c6-3405-9dc6-421d740cc6c3",
                        "entry_id": "cdc9f64b-a5b8-3aaf-819b-4249388c7a5f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ce à quoi le signe (le mot, l'expression) fait référence et que l'on peut trouver dans le dictionnaire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac70e501-e461-42f7-b09b-b523c7b70793",
                                "sense_id": "9a00c8f3-e1c6-3405-9dc6-421d740cc6c3",
                                "text": "Si je puis être un peu technique un instant, il s'agit de savoir si parmi les pages d'un journal intime on parle dans la dénotation (le sens officiel, celui des dictionnaires) ou bien dans la connotation (le sens parasite, les allusions, l'épaisseur historique des mots). Ainsi des participants réguliers d'une émission de radio, on dit qu'il en sont les collaborateurs. C'est la dénotation. Mais le mot connote mal. Je m'en suis insuffisamment avisé, parce que rien n'était plus éloigné de ma pensée que le lourd passé de ce terme. Cependant, si l'on exige de nous que nous parlions, écrivions et vivions exclusivement dans la connotation, on ne peut plus faire de cure à Vichy, ni aimer la campagne de France car depuis que « la terre, elle, ne ment pas », elle est devenue très suspecte."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "55405847-cfc8-46e0-a937-ea8d5b3030d8",
                        "source_entry_id": "cdc9f64b-a5b8-3aaf-819b-4249388c7a5f",
                        "source_sense_id": "934ada64-79ce-372d-8bc5-87f421fd39e9",
                        "target_lang_word": "denotation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "denotation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3d7fd019-44ad-39eb-bd46-d551d897a379",
                                        "entry_id": "739addfd-32a5-36b3-a647-64a3f64c1b13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of denoting, or something (such as a symbol) that denotes"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d040ce18-e0f2-3ab0-ad3b-397bb9a3da4f",
                                        "entry_id": "739addfd-32a5-36b3-a647-64a3f64c1b13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The primary, surface, literal, or explicit meaning of a signifier such as a word, phrase, or symbol; that which a word denotes, as contrasted with its connotation; the aggregate or set of objects of which a word may be predicated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25380090-d59a-4d9c-a953-4b73b3818f48",
                                                "sense_id": "d040ce18-e0f2-3ab0-ad3b-397bb9a3da4f",
                                                "text": "The denotations of the two expressions \"the morning star\" and \"the evening star\" are the same (i.e. both expressions denote the planet Venus), but their connotations are different."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84463789-30f6-40e4-9599-0ef24d770161",
                                                "sense_id": "d040ce18-e0f2-3ab0-ad3b-397bb9a3da4f",
                                                "text": "Regarding denotation, the terms were generally used to refer to a wide range of language contact varieties and features."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf0461b0-edc3-3a6d-967a-fd654628b438",
                                        "entry_id": "739addfd-32a5-36b3-a647-64a3f64c1b13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The intension and extension of a word"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "15006435-f951-34bd-80ed-6ac92074a3e4",
                                        "entry_id": "739addfd-32a5-36b3-a647-64a3f64c1b13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something signified or referred to; a particular meaning of a symbol"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "279ca0e0-6f45-3e26-81b9-c78af57a5c7f",
                                        "entry_id": "739addfd-32a5-36b3-a647-64a3f64c1b13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any mathematical object which describes the meanings of expressions from the languages, formalized in the theory of denotational semantics"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c8e4102-1291-3476-856d-23990edb4ed2",
                                        "entry_id": "739addfd-32a5-36b3-a647-64a3f64c1b13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A first level of analysis: what the audience can visually see on a page. Denotation often refers to something literal, and avoids being a metaphor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
